# ============================================================
# Example: hardened sshd_config — Linux (Ubuntu/Debian)
# Tested on: OpenSSH 9.x
# Adjust before applying: the port, the allowed group (AllowGroups) and the banner path.
# Related best practice: best-practices/general/ssh-hardening.md
# Apply: copy to /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/99-netops.conf and run 'systemctl reload ssh'.
# WARNING: make sure your public key is already installed BEFORE turning off passwords.
# ============================================================

Port 22

# --- Authentication: keys yes, passwords no, root without password ---
PubkeyAuthentication yes
PasswordAuthentication no
PermitRootLogin prohibit-password
PermitEmptyPasswords no

# --- Limits against brute force ---
MaxAuthTries 3
LoginGraceTime 30
MaxSessions 4

# --- Idle session: dropped after ~10 min ---
ClientAliveInterval 300
ClientAliveCountMax 2

# --- Reduce the surface ---
X11Forwarding no
AllowTcpForwarding no
AllowAgentForwarding no

# --- Restrict who can log in (create the group: groupadd ssh-users) ---
AllowGroups ssh-users

# --- Modern cryptography ---
KexAlgorithms curve25519-sha256,curve25519-sha256@libssh.org
Ciphers chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com,aes256-gcm@openssh.com
MACs hmac-sha2-512-etm@openssh.com,hmac-sha2-256-etm@openssh.com

# --- Legal notice ---
Banner /etc/issue.net
